      "project_id": 34675721,
      "title": "perf(api): reuse connections across API clients",
      "description": "## Description\n\n* perf(api): keep up to 25 idle connections per host\n\nClients from one factory now share a transport, so concurrent fan-out\n(MRsFromArgs, IssuesFromArgs) draws on a single pool. Go's default of\ntwo idle connections per host closed the rest after each round and made\nthe next round dial again over HTTP/1.1.\n\n* perf(api): reuse connections across API clients\n\nEvery api.NewClient call built its own http.Transport, so each\nFactory.GitLabClient() / Factory.ApiClient() call paid for a new TCP and\nTLS handshake. `glab mr view 1` used three connections for its three\nrequests (MR lookup, approvals, telemetry).\n\nThe factory now owns an api.TransportCache, and clients it builds share\none transport whenever their transport settings (proxy, CA, client\ncertificate, skip_tls_verify, gitlab.com cipher suites) match. A\nper-client wrapper hides CloseIdleConnections, which go-retryablehttp\ncalls after failed requests, so one client cannot drain the shared pool.\nClients built outside the factory keep a private transport.\n\nAt 50ms RTT against a mock GitLab: mr view 399ms -> 275ms,\nmr list 276ms -> 214ms.\n\n## Related Issues\n\n## How has this been tested?",
